AgriTwin Rwanda — NOTICE

Submission for the NISR 2026 Big Data Hackathon, Track 1 (Agricultural Productivity).

IP transfer
-----------
Per the NISR 2026 Big Data Hackathon rules, intellectual property in this submission
(including all original code, documentation, models, and derived outputs produced by the
team for this project) transfers to the National Institute of Statistics of Rwanda (NISR)
upon submission, as required by the hackathon's terms of participation. This NOTICE exists
to record that transfer alongside the project itself; it does not itself restate the full
text of the hackathon rules, which govern.

This repository does not (and, per `.gitignore` and `CLAUDE.md` golden rule 1, must never)
contain raw or plot-level NISR microdata. Only aggregated, district-level outputs are
committed. See `AI_DISCLOSURE.md` for AI-tool usage disclosure and `ORIGINALITY.md` for the
team's declaration of original work.

Third-party data sources and licenses
--------------------------------------
Full source records, catalog IDs, and access notes are maintained in
`config/data_sources.yaml` (NISR microdata, Earth Engine datasets) and
`docs/data-sources.md` (HDX boundaries). Summary:

- **NISR Seasonal Agricultural Survey (SAS) 2019-2025 and Agriculture Household Survey
  (AHS) 2024.** Source: National Institute of Statistics of Rwanda microdata catalog
  (`https://www.microdata.statistics.gov.rw`). Subject to NISR's own microdata access and
  use terms (login and, for some years, approval required to download). Not redistributed
  in this repository in any raw or identifiable form; only aggregated, district-level
  statistics derived from it appear in `data/public/`.

- **MODIS NDVI/EVI** (`MODIS/061/MOD13Q1`), **Sentinel-2 SR** (`COPERNICUS/S2_SR_HARMONIZED`),
  **CHIRPS daily rainfall** (`UCSB-CHG/CHIRPS/DAILY`), **ESA WorldCover** (`ESA/WorldCover/v200`),
  **iSDAsoil** (`ISDASOIL/Africa/v1/*`), **SRTM elevation** (`USGS/SRTMGL1_003`). Accessed via
  Google Earth Engine under Earth Engine's noncommercial/academic terms of use. See each
  dataset's entry in Earth Engine's public data catalog (`developers.google.com/earth-engine/datasets`)
  for its specific license; this project does not redistribute the raw imagery, only derived
  district-level zonal statistics.

- **Rwanda administrative boundaries (COD-AB), admin level 2.** Source: UN OCHA Common
  Operational Datasets, `https://data.humdata.org/dataset/cod-ab-rwa`, originally sourced from
  NISR and vetted by ITOS (USAID-funded). License: **Creative Commons Attribution for
  Intergovernmental Organisations (CC BY-IGO)**. Downloaded 2026-09-23; see
  `docs/data-sources.md` for the exact resource URL. A simplified derivative is committed at
  `data/public/geo/districts_adm2.geojson`.

- **FAO GAUL districts** (`FAO/GAUL/2015/level2`), accessed via Earth Engine, used as the
  original boundary source for `data/external/gee/*.csv` (see `docs/decisions.md`
  2026-09-23 for why both GAUL and HDX boundaries are retained side by side). Subject to
  FAO GAUL's own terms; see the dataset's Earth Engine catalog entry.

